{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":105686,"duration_api_ms":157927,"num_turns":6,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6edb2034-0f35-4969-8603-cf8315b5a92e","total_cost_usd":0.4702632,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27849,"cache_read_input_tokens":82090,"output_tokens":2559,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27849,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":147,"outputTokens":8258,"cacheReadInputTokens":684862,"cacheCreationInputTokens":64995,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.19116695,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2559,"cacheReadInputTokens":82090,"cacheCreationInputTokens":27849,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.27909625,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All seven amendments are verified against the source code and identify genuine issues. Five address hardcoded model coefficients or diagnostic thresholds that violate the stated acceptance criteria of named parameters, and two identify integration tests that overclaim their coverage. I agree with all planner positions.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-6-659b3f63","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: 0.3 increment (line 649) and 0.35 decrement (line 653) are literal constants with no corresponding fields in ShrimpRuntimeParams. These directly govern failed_molt_accum dynamics, which feeds both stress and mortality. The acceptance criteria explicitly requires all molt-related thresholds and modifiers to be named parameters. Promoting these to ShrimpRuntimeParams and neocaridina_davidi.toml is straightforward and necessary."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-1c45f0d3","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: ro_like.toml has calcium_mg_per_l = 20.0 and magnesium_mg_per_l = 5.0, which exactly match the species defaults ca_min_mg_per_l = 20.0 and mg_min_mg_per_l = 5.0 in neocaridina_davidi.toml and biology.rs defaults. This means both mineral subfactors compute to 1.0 (no penalty), so the integration test only exercises the GH penalty path. To verify that Ca and Mg individually contribute to the mineral modifier in an integrated setting, the test needs a profile with values below those minimums."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-b71a2aad","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: lines 1362-1368 show an unconditional fallback to EventCause::PoorCondition when causes is empty. A marginal failure where success_score narrowly misses the threshold due to multiple slightly-suboptimal factors—none crossing their individual diagnostic thresholds—will be mislabeled as PoorCondition. This is a real user-facing diagnostic issue. Adding a MarginalFailure cause or including the success_score gap in the event details would give the player actionable information."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-fe4cee4a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: instability threshold 0.3 at line 1337 and condition threshold 0.65 at line 621 are raw literals that gate which EventCause codes are emitted. These are player-visible diagnostic decision points. At minimum they should be named constants for auditability; ideally they'd be configurable alongside the other molt parameters, consistent with the project's parameterization philosophy."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-7ab7e2a1","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: line 676 shows `failed_molt_accum * 0.5` feeding into molt_stress_index, which then contributes to stress_total via `(molt_stress_index - 0.5).max(0.0)` at line 1178. The direct channel at line 1184 uses the parameterized failed_molt_mortality_scale. The code comments acknowledge the dual-channel design is intentional, but the 0.5 blending factor is a hardcoded tuning knob that materially affects the combined mortality rate. It should be a named parameter for consistency with the rest of the molt model."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-86390c91","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: run_day() calls step_hours(24), and the test captures snapshot() once after the full 24-hour block. max_tan, max_no2, and max_instability are only updated from that single end-of-day reading. Any intra-day excursion that settles before the snapshot is invisible. The test's assertions about 'keeping chemistry in range' overstate the coverage they actually provide."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-faf7e3a2","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the test drives temperature to 36°C which simultaneously causes: (1) elevated instability_index, (2) a direct temperature penalty on readiness, and (3) heat stress affecting condition and molt outcomes. The test asserts instability remains elevated and readiness stays suppressed, but never demonstrates that instability is the causal mechanism. The 36°C shock creates multiple confounded effects—the test would pass even if instability_index were completely disconnected from readiness, as long as temperature or condition penalties persisted."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"5f672763-77ff-4a76-aa18-4e4cbc4afafa"}
